<title>JAPAN: Japan's DIC to give Tokai Bank Y169.7 bln.</title>
<headline>Japan's DIC to give Tokai Bank Y169.7 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Deposit Insurance Corporation (DIC) said on Thursday it would provide 169.7 billion yen to Tokai Bank for the bank's takeover of the healthy assets of failed credit union Osaka Shinyo Kumiai.</p>
<p>Tokai Bank is expected to take over Osaka Kumiai on January 10.</p>
<p>Non-performing assets at Osaka Kumiai will be transferred to the Resolution and Collection Bank Ltd (RCB), a body responsible for managing and collecting bad loans of failed credit unions.</p>
</text>
